## Report

1. **What was failing and why:** The `dedup_inplace` function had a use-after-free bug. When the "best" (earliest-input) representative was not at the first position of its group, the code copied the struct to `c->lines[n]` and then the subsequent free loop would free `c->lines[n].data` (same pointer as the kept line's data) because `n` fell within the `[i, j)` range and `n != best`. This caused heap corruption → SIGABRT/SIGTRAP.

2. **What I changed:** Reordered the operations in `dedup_inplace`: save the kept `Line` into a local variable first, free all non-kept data in the group, then write the local into `c->lines[n]`. This eliminates the use-after-free.

3. **Build command run:** `mkdir -p build && cc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -pedantic -O2 src/new_sort/new_sort.c -o build/new_sort` — passed with no warnings.

4. **Which failing tests I expect to pass now:** All four — `adv-manylines-u.p`, `pair-f-u-discrim.p`, `single-u-x-generic.p`, `single-u-x-generic.r` — were all crashing due to this same memory corruption bug in `dedup_inplace`.
